{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The voice of words you heard.</b> The verse's saying <b>the voice of words</b> may be explained according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:2), who said that every utterance that went forth from the mouth of HaShem, an angel was formed from it, and it would stand over each person and say to him: ״Do you accept me?״ and so on, and it would embrace him, and so on — end of quotation. According to this, the verse is explained precisely: <b>the voice of words</b> — meaning, the words that HaShem spoke, from which angels were created; the voice of those angels, who are called ״words,״ is what you heard. And see what I wrote in parashat Yitro, that Israel heard from the mouth of the Gevurah only ״אָנֹכִי״ etc. and ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״ etc.; but the eight commandments — even though all ten came forth together as one, they could not endure to hear more than two, and for the remaining eight the angels that were hewn from His voice, may He be blessed, stood with them until their soul returned, and then they heard them again from the mouth of the angels — which are the ״words״ themselves; and each and every commandment, which was an angel and an angel, would stand over each person and say to him: ״Do you accept me?״ and so on." "<b>And no likeness did you see, etc.</b> It is difficult: how can it be justified to say about a likeness that it is <b>save a voice</b> — which is the hearing? And according to what I wrote in the preceding verse, that the angel, which is the utterance itself, was speaking with each person and Israel would see it — and so you will find that our Sages of blessed memory said (Mekhilta, Exodus 20:15) on the verse ״וְכָל הָעָם רֹאִים אֶת הַקּוֹלוֹת״ — from this Moses was concerned lest they think, heaven forbid, that this is the God of Israel whom their eyes beheld; therefore he said <b>and no likeness did you see, save a voice</b> — meaning: apart from the voice, it was its likeness that you would see, which was speaking with you and saying ״Do you accept me?״ and so on."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:12.504607261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}